{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_nfmnsgil6fdwp3e22jfmknux3pshs6fg7umjyb2xp7sxgt7dfwta","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 39 tests pass. Summary of what I did:\n\n## Phase 1: Translation\n\nImplemented all `unimplemented!()` stubs as safe, idiomatic Rust (no `unsafe`, no FFI):\n\n- **`src/tableau.rs`** — `beaufort_tableau` builds a square tableau where `mat[y][x] = alpha[(size + y - x) % size]`, mirroring the C loop with `j = size, ++x, --j`.\n- **`src/encrypt.rs`** — `beaufort_encrypt` finds the column where `mat[0][x] == ch`, then the row where `mat[y][x] == key[j]`, and emits `mat[y][0]`. Non-alphabet chars pass through and don't advance the key index, matching C's `j--` rollback.\n- **`src/decrypt.rs`** — `beaufort_decrypt` is the inverse: locate the row where `mat[y][0] == ch`, then the column where `mat[y][x] == key[j]`, and emit `mat[0][x]`.\n- **`src/lib.rs`** — `ssize` (counts bytes up to first NUL), `usage`/`help` (stderr), `read_stdin`, and a CLI `main()` that parses `--encrypt`, `--decrypt`, `--key=`, `--alphabet=`, `-h`, `-V`. When `mat` is empty, encrypt/decrypt fall back to the default `BEAUFORT_ALPHA` tableau.\n\n`cargo build` succeeds with no errors.\n\n## Phase 2: Tests\n\nBuilt the C reference binary and used its outputs to drive assertions across four test files in `src/bin/` covering every module in `lib.rs`:\n\n- `test_tableau.rs` — 7 tests (default alphabet sizes/contents, `AB`, `ABCDE`, single-char `X`, `ABCDEFGHIJ`, first-column equals alphabet)\n- `test_encrypt.rs` — 13 tests (canonical strings, punctuation/whitespace pass-through, empty input, key length variations, custom small alphabets, reciprocity)\n- `test_decrypt.rs` — 13 tests (mirror of encrypt + reciprocal verification)\n- `test_lib.rs` — 6 tests (constants, `ssize` for empty/normal/embedded-NUL strings)\n\n`cargo test` reports **39 passed; 0 failed** across all four binaries."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop